WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
You have one free evening.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.790
Every hour of homework
is an hour you can't

3
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:06.320
spend at your job.

4
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.650
Whole countries face the same trade-off,

5
00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.470
on a giant scale.

6
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:14.030
Picture an economy that
makes only food and machines.

7
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.800
A graph can show every efficient mix.

8
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.600
So why can each extra
machine cost the country

9
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.890
more food than the one before?

10
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:26.780
In this mission, you'll calculate opportunity
cost from a table and compare straight,

11
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.290
bowed-out and bowed-in curves.

12
00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:32.270
Then you'll test what makes
the curve shift outward,

13
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.220
like better technology, and inward.

14
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.970
Your mission: figure out
what the shape of the curve

15
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.910
tells you about every
trade-off a country makes.
